# U-Boot environment location on the SSC30KQ.
#
# mtd1 is the environment under both the OEM table and the one this tree
# generates, and both give it the same offset and size, so this file is correct
# before and after the partition change:
#
#   dev:    size     erasesize  name
#   mtd0: 00040000  00010000  "boot"
#   mtd1: 00010000  00010000  "env"      <- this file
#   mtd2: 00200000  00010000  "kernel"
#   mtd3: <sized>   00010000  "rootfs"
#   mtd4: <rest>    00010000  "data"     ("rootfs_data" under the OEM table)
#   mtd5: 01000000  00010000  "all"      (generated table only)
#
# The kernel and rootfs partitions are sized to the built images, so anything
# quoting a fixed size for mtd3 onward is quoting one particular build. The
# authority is /proc/mtd on the running unit.
#
# thingino's base overlay/etc/fw_env.config declares a 0x8000 sector, which is
# right for the Ingenic boards it was written for and wrong here: this NOR chip
# erases in 64KB blocks. fw_setenv's write path erases one DEVESIZE chunk at a
# time, so a 0x8000 length reaches MEMERASE unaligned and the ioctl rejects it.
# thingino-sysupgrade (S97sysupgrade) and the WebUI both call fw_setenv, so this
# is a live path, not a theoretical one.
#
# Overridden per-camera rather than by editing the base overlay: Makefile:598
# appends this directory to BR2_ROOTFS_OVERLAY after the shared one, so the file
# here wins with zero merge surface upstream.
#
# <device> <offset> <env size> <sector size>
/dev/mtd1 0x0 0x10000 0x10000
